\begin{figure}[t]
\centering\vspace{-3pt}
\includegraphics[width=0.95\columnwidth]{fig_seed_variability.pdf}\vspace{-5pt}
\caption{OOD success rate across 11 episode-level GRPO seeds (Wilson 95\% CI). Seeds partition into \textit{Generalized} ($p{<}0.01$ vs.\ SFT), \textit{Stagnant} (stable, NS), and \textit{Collapsed} ($\times$). Avoiding collapse is necessary but not sufficient.}
\label{fig:seed_variability}\vspace{-8pt}
\end{figure}

Three distinct outcomes emerge (Table~\ref{tab:seed_variability}, Figure~\ref{fig:seed_variability}): roughly a quarter of seeds collapse with response length inflation (Appendix~\ref{app:response_length}), a third are stagnant with OOD performance indistinguishable from SFT, and a third generalize with significant OOD improvement. No collapsed seed generalizes, and training duration does not explain the gap between stagnant and generalized seeds. Stable training is necessary but not sufficient; the mechanism driving seed-dependent transfer remains an open question (Section~\ref{sec:discussion}).% exp_id: exp029 multi-seed series

\subsection{Cross-Scale and Cross-Environment Verification}
\label{sec:cross_scale}

A single-seed 8B experiment confirms both failure and fix persist at scale: Cell~A collapses within two steps while Cell~D reaches 90.3\% OOD (Appendix~\ref{app:8b_results}); restricting to $h{=}2$ confirms severe information loss. The pathology is environment-general: step-independent training on ScienceWorld~\cite{wang2022scienceworld} also collapses to 0\% across all 15 steps with comparable M1 gap.% exp_id: 8b_cell_c_episode_v9d, 8b_v9d_ood_eval_v5, scienceworld_grpo_cell_a, sw_info_loss_bjb1

